{
  "uid": "governed-run-lifecycle",
  "title": "Governed Run Lifecycle (15.1)",
  "tags": [
    "governed",
    "15.1",
    "agentops",
    "trace"
  ],
  "timezone": "browser",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "version": 1,
  "refresh": "30s",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-24h",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "templating": {
    "list": [
      {
        "name": "trace_id",
        "label": "trace_id",
        "type": "textbox",
        "query": "",
        "current": {
          "text": "",
          "value": ""
        },
        "description": "The W3C trace_id that keys the whole run across ClickHouse spans, Loki events and the Postgres audit chain. Paste the demo run's trace_id."
      },
      {
        "name": "run_id",
        "label": "run_id",
        "type": "textbox",
        "query": "",
        "current": {
          "text": "",
          "value": ""
        },
        "description": "The controller run_id (== AGENTPACK_CONTRACT_ID). Filters the same events by contract_id when trace_id is not to hand."
      }
    ]
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "About",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Governed run lifecycle**, keyed on a single `trace_id` / `run_id`. Every governed hop (`agentops emit`) carries the controller-minted `trace_id`+`contract_id`, so filtering `{job=\"agentops\"}` by them replays the whole chain from one store. The SAME `trace_id` keys the ClickHouse `spans_v1` and the same `run_id` keys the Postgres `audit_events` chain (see RUNBOOK.md \u00a7\"Read a trace across the three stores\"). Set the `trace_id` variable (top-left) to the demo run's id.\n\n---\n\n**Empty is not broken (verified 2026-08-27).** Every query here targets `job=\"agentops\"`, written by `agent-pack/bin/agentops-ship.py` (`dispatch | escalation | verdict | adhoc | dispatch_start`). That vocabulary is correct and the shipper is installed \u2014 but no governed agent-pack run has executed inside Loki's 7-day retention (the only `agentops` line in the window is a `test_governed_fleet_probe` from 2026-08-26). So these panels read *No data* because the fleet has been idle on this path, **not** because the queries are wrong. Run a governed card and they populate. If they are still empty after a run, the shipper is not reaching Loki \u2014 check `agentops-ship.py --loki`."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Governed events (this trace)",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "loki",
        "uid": "loki"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 7
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ]
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "loki",
            "uid": "loki"
          },
          "expr": "sum(count_over_time({job=\"agentops\"} |= \"$trace_id\" [$__range]))",
          "queryType": "instant"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "PMO gate decisions",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "loki",
        "uid": "loki"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 6,
        "y": 7
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "color": {
